concept:
Sometimes you count both ways: parts IN vs parts OUT of a buffer, cars entering
and leaving a lot, bottles added and removed. That's an up-down counter (CTUD).

Do it with a rising-edge one-shot on each input (see Lesson 9):

    IF In_Sensor  AND NOT In_Prev  THEN Count := Count + 1; END_IF;
    IF Out_Sensor AND NOT Out_Prev THEN Count := Count - 1; END_IF;
    In_Prev := In_Sensor;  Out_Prev := Out_Sensor;

Count now tracks how many are currently in the buffer.

solution:
(* Lesson 10 -- Up-Down Counter (CTUD) *)

VAR
    In_Sensor  : BOOL;  (* N.O. entry photo-eye -> XIC (as-is) *)
    Out_Sensor : BOOL;  (* N.O. exit photo-eye  -> XIC (as-is) *)
    In_Prev    : BOOL;  (* entry edge memory                   *)
    Out_Prev   : BOOL;  (* exit edge memory                    *)
    Count      : DINT;  (* output: items currently in buffer   *)
END_VAR

(* ----- YOUR LOGIC : write your answer between these two lines ----- *)
IF In_Sensor AND NOT In_Prev THEN
    Count := Count + 1;
END_IF;
IF Out_Sensor AND NOT Out_Prev THEN
    Count := Count - 1;
END_IF;
In_Prev := In_Sensor;
Out_Prev := Out_Sensor;
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *)
